WEBVTT

00:00:01.880 --> 00:00:05.480
This is the Transhuman Daily, for Monday, November 2.

00:00:06.560 --> 00:00:10.990
Here are the last 24 hours in transhumanism, in 3 minutes.

00:00:15.000 --> 00:00:17.880
The week's best? It's never too late.

00:00:17.880 --> 00:00:21.840
Old mice given an enzyme blocker lived 17% longer.

00:00:22.030 --> 00:00:22.980
Closer to home,

00:00:22.980 --> 00:00:27.160
Monash found retiring didn't make older Australians any lonelier.

00:00:31.880 --> 00:00:32.320
In AI,

00:00:32.320 --> 00:00:38.440
an agent reading abdominal ultrasounds got the diagnosis right 99.6% of the time.

00:00:39.380 --> 00:00:43.620
Elon Musk says Neuralink's Blindsight, an implant aimed at blindness,

00:00:43.620 --> 00:00:46.200
is ready. Regulators still have to agree.

00:00:46.410 --> 00:00:50.200
Trouble is, implants fade as the brain scars around them.

00:00:50.200 --> 00:00:53.130
A five-year Miami study wants them to last.

00:00:53.440 --> 00:00:57.710
And 50 AI agents, told to build a Minecraft civilization,

00:00:57.710 --> 00:00:59.880
built a bureaucracy instead.

00:01:00.000 --> 00:01:01.390
In the longevity lab,

00:01:01.390 --> 00:01:06.370
a vaccine against worn-out 'zombie' cells helped old mice live 12% longer.

00:01:07.500 --> 00:01:09.300
And Britain cleared Casgevy,

00:01:09.300 --> 00:01:14.500
a gene-editing treatment for two inherited blood disorders, for kids from age 5.

00:01:15.000 --> 00:01:19.290
Seniors who napped most days had a 48% higher dementia rate.

00:01:19.290 --> 00:01:21.220
Maybe a sign, not a cause.

00:01:22.500 --> 00:01:28.780
Plus, the Dog Aging Project won US$29 million to learn why some dogs age better.

00:01:30.000 --> 00:01:31.290
In a mid-stage trial,

00:01:31.290 --> 00:01:36.340
one dose of a psychedelic nasal spray eased hard-to-treat depression for 8 weeks.

00:01:37.500 --> 00:01:40.950
And Australia's biggest study of wellbeing and ageing acro

00:01:40.950 --> 00:01:44.460
ss generations starts recruiting 100,000 people this month.

00:01:45.000 --> 00:01:50.470
Now, the catch. An Alzheimer's drug lowered plaque but didn't slow decline,

00:01:50.470 --> 00:01:52.720
in a trial of over 500 people.

00:01:52.970 --> 00:01:56.690
And AI translation sounds fluent, but isn't always right.

00:01:56.690 --> 00:01:59.380
One turned Aussie thongs into underwear.

00:02:01.880 --> 00:02:05.480
Meanwhile, SpaceX flew Falcon 9 for the 700th time,

00:02:05.480 --> 00:02:08.100
and the booster landed at sea again.

00:02:09.380 --> 00:02:14.730
One recent passenger, Google's AI satellite, just wrote a haiku from orbit.

00:02:15.940 --> 00:02:16.870
In Hangzhou,

00:02:16.870 --> 00:02:22.540
a humanoid robot traffic cop helped patrol a marathon of 36,000 runners.

00:02:22.500 --> 00:02:24.460
Old mice, old dogs, new tricks.

00:02:24.460 --> 00:02:28.430
It's never too late to start something new. Even a daily show.

00:02:30.000 --> 00:02:32.950
Day after day, the curve keeps bending upward.

00:02:33.750 --> 00:02:36.710
Somehow, the future keeps landing early.

00:02:37.500 --> 00:02:41.350
That's one day of news. Imagine what a year looks like.

00:02:45.000 --> 00:02:47.100
This has been the Transhuman Daily.

00:02:48.750 --> 00:02:51.330
Stay well. Same time tomorrow?

00:02:52.500 --> 00:02:56.600
Want more? Meet us in North Sydney on November 27.
